schema: "0.4"
id: chalkboard-12-profile-manager
type: image
quality: high

# The Robot Learns — a terminal study CLI. Profile Manager — manage named profile lifecycle
# (switch/rename/export) and clean uninstall, rendered as a chalkboard terminal.
# Theme tenets: always-dark forest-green slate board, warm chalk-white hand-lettering, dusty
# colored-chalk accents used categorically (never neon), flat radius-0 board, dashed chalk
# rules + hand-drawn underline for the active item (never bold weight); destructive action in
# rose chalk reinforced with an underline/icon since rose is both a brand and the error hue.
# Palette: board green #2d4a2d, near-black board #1e2a1e, chalk-white #e8e4d8, sand-chalk
# #c8c0a8, yellow chalk #e8d44c, blue chalk #6cb4dc, rose chalk #e06060, sage chalk #50b878.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a warm,
    always-dark TERMINAL session skinned as a professor's chalkboard — a single focused
    terminal window, not a web page and not a browser. The surface is a calm settings board for
    managing named study profiles: a short written list of profiles the way a teacher keeps a
    roster, with the current one circled. Names and prompts are hand-lettered in a casual
    print-handwriting face; paths and keys stay in a neat monospace. Emphasis is an underline,
    never a bold weight. Colored chalk is dusty and desaturated, never neon. Flat board, square
    corners, dashed chalk rules, a faint dust of chalk texture. Minimal and unhurried.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity mockup of a focused single-pane TERMINAL session — "The Robot
    Learns" — skinned as a dark green chalkboard, showing the profile manager. One warm
    forest-green slate board fills the frame like a terminal window. NO browser chrome, NO tabs,
    NO address bar, NO web page.

    OVERALL LAYOUT: a written board title, a calm central roster of named profiles, and a
    guarded action row at the bottom.

    TOP is a board title in display handwriting, "Profiles", with a dashed chalk rule under it.

    The dominant CENTER is the PROFILE SELECTOR — a short roster of named profiles, each a row.
    The row shows the profile name in chalk-white, "work" and "personal-learning" and "french-
    tutor", and a couple of small EXPERTISE LEVEL BADGES per profile drawn as chalk-outlined
    tags in different colored chalk, "Algorithms · Expert" in sage, "French · Beginner" in blue.
    The active "work" profile is marked by a bright yellow-chalk underline and slightly larger
    lettering, like the current topic circled on the board; rows are divided by dashed chalk
    rules.

    A guarded ACTION ROW near the bottom lists chalk-outlined actions "switch · rename · export
    kb · uninstall"; the destructive "uninstall" is drawn in dusty rose chalk with an underline
    and a small warning tick so it does not read as ordinary red chalk. A CONFIRMATION PROMPT is
    a hand-drawn chalk-outlined box guarding it, a written line "Remove 'work' and keep its
    board? your KB is exported first", with two chalk choices "[ export + remove ]" and
    "[ cancel ]". A faint monospace status line reads "profiles live in ~/.config/the-robot-
    learns-kb".

    PALETTE & TYPE: a deep forest-green slate board as the canvas, one slightly lighter green
    panel for the confirmation box; lettering in warm dusty chalk-white, secondary labels in
    dimmer sand-chalk. Badges and the active mark in sticks of dusty colored chalk — a warm
    butter-yellow for the active underline, a sage green and a dusty sky-blue for badges, a soft
    rose-red for the destructive action — all desaturated like real chalk, never bright or neon.
    Names and prompts hand-lettered in a casual print handwriting face; the path and keys in a
    neat monospace.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: flat board with square corners, no rounded cards and no glossy panels;
    roster rows divided by dashed chalk rules; badges and the confirmation box are hand-drawn
    chalk outlines with slightly uneven edges; a faint even dust of chalk grain and one soft
    eraser smudge.

    MOOD: warm, academic, personal — a tidy roster kept in a careful hand, calm and minimal, the
    quiet housekeeping of a good classroom.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, browser chrome, address bar, browser tabs, web page, rounded cards, glossy panels, neon or saturated colors, dry-erase whiteboard, pure white or light background, bold heavy type"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches Profile Manager: a roster of named profiles with per-profile expertise badges, an active-profile marker, a guarded action row (switch/rename/export/uninstall), and a confirmation prompt on the destructive action — inside one terminal board"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Always-dark forest-green board, warm chalk-white handwriting names + mono path, dusty categorical colored-chalk badges and a yellow active underline (no neon), destructive action in rose reinforced with underline/icon, flat square corners, dashed chalk rules — not generic UI defaults"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Calm minimal roster hierarchy with a guarded action row, plausible real-product terminal settings layout"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "browser chrome, tabs, or address bar instead of a terminal window"
    - "neon or saturated colors, or a light/whiteboard background"

tags: [chalkboard, therobotlearns.com, screen-mockup, terminal]
